## Building on Linux

```sh
make clean && make && make test
```

## Building on Windows (MSYS2 UCRT64)

**Recommended:** open **MSYS2 UCRT64** from the Start menu:

```sh
pacman -S make mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-gcc   # once
cd /path/to/cat-toto
make clean && make && make test
```

Produces a **native Windows executable** (`cat-toto` or `cat-toto.exe`).
Runs in UCRT64, Git Bash, and CMD.

### Git Bash caveat

Git Bash can build if **`/c/msys64/ucrt64/bin` is early on `PATH`** (before
Anaconda). Otherwise `gcc --version` may work while `cc1` fails silently (DLL
load order). Prefer UCRT64 shell or:

```bash
PATH="/c/msys64/ucrt64/bin:$PATH" make
```

## Linking notes

- `cat_toto_format_chunk()` and `cat_toto_format_state_init()` are defined in
  `src/cat_toto_format.c` and linked into **both** the main binary and the test
  binary.
- Tests link `src/cat_toto_format.c` **directly**; they do **not** link
  `src/main.c`, `src/cat_toto_io.c`, `src/cat_toto_cli.c`, or
  `src/cat_toto_emit.c`.
- `main()` lives only in `src/main.c`.
- `snprintf` is used inside `cat_toto_format.c` for line number formatting only;
  it is **not** used for I/O. All actual I/O goes through `read(2)` /
  `write(2)`.

